exit: 2
--- stdout

--- stderr
✗ --reason is required — say what is wrong.

commandments report — File a GitHub issue about code-commandments itself (via `gh`) — a false positive, a wrong rule, or a bug.

Usage:
  commandments report --reason="…" --ref=PATH:LINE
                                    a [bug-report] — a defect in the tool, pointing at the code it
                                    happened on
  commandments report follow        ask GitHub what became of every report this project filed, and
                                    what to do about each answer
  commandments report forget ISSUE  drop a report once its answer is settled, so its sin is judged
                                    as any other again
  commandments report accept ISSUE --why="…"
                                    keep a report whose fix this project cannot take yet, so nothing
                                    asks about it again
  commandments report --detector=NAME --reason="…" --ref=PATH:LINE
                                    a [detector-report] — this finding is a false positive

Options:
  --reason="…"          what is wrong (required)
  --ref=PATH:LINE       the code this is about — repeatable, and PATH:START-END works; the issue
                        names the file and its lines
  --share-code          also show the referenced lines (those alone, secrets masked) — only when
                        the project's owner agrees its code may be public
  --detector=NAME       the detector that fired — makes this a false-positive report
  --best-design="…"     the cleanest design you can conceive for the flagged code; REQUIRED by
                        design-smell detectors
  --title="…"           the issue title (default: the reason's first line)
  --global              opt out of --ref when the defect is tied to no file at all (a crash with no
                        args, a CLI-wide bug)
  --why="…"             with `report accept`: why the answer cannot be acted on, which the dashboard
                        shows beside the row
  --file=PATH --line=N  the single-ref alias for --ref

  Only rules the PACKAGE ships can be reported here. A finding printed as `[Name (custom)]` comes
  from a detector this project wrote into .commandments/custom/ — fix it there; a report against
  it is refused.

  Filing a detector-report RECORDS the sin it was about in .commandments/reports.json, which is
  tracked: a judge of that line then reads it as reported, with its issue, rather than as a sin to
  fix, and `report follow` says when the report has been answered. The line's own text is kept as a
  hash, never as text, and a second report of a sin already recorded is refused.

  A report is NOT a deferral. A correct finding must be FIXED, however big the fix — a
  detector-report asserts flatly that the code is right and the rule is wrong, with no hedge. Some
  detectors (design smells) REQUIRE --best-design: the report is valid only when the flagged code
  ALREADY IS that best design.

